[ti:Day 23]

[00:00.00]flexible [ˈfleksəbl]a. 弯曲的；灵活的；有弹性的；可变 通的 例 We should stick to the principles and be flexible as well.
[00:10.44]guarantee [ˌɡærənˈtiː]vt. 保证；担保 n. 保证；保证书；保 单；担保人；抵押品 例 The makers guarantee this special glass is unbreakable. 搭 guarantee sb. against 保证…免受损害 / stand guarantee for sb. 替某人作保
[00:28.44]bootleg [ˈbuːtleɡ]v. 非法贩运，走私；非法生产 n. 靴 筒；私货 例 The country's bootleg alcohol reportedly generated fabulous wealth every year.
[00:41.40]wary [ˈweəri]a. 谨慎的；警惕的；谨防的 搭 be wary of 提防 / keep a wary eye on sb. 密切注意某人 / wary tactics 谨慎的策略 profit and loss account 损益账户
[00:53.52]hint [hɪnt]n. 暗示，示意；细微的迹象；[常pl.] 建议 v. 暗示 例 The director threw out a hint regarding bonuses at the end of the year. 搭 drop a hint 给人暗示，露口风 / hint at 暗示 / take a hint 接受别人的暗示；领会
[01:10.56]pilferage [ˈpɪlfərɪdʒ]n. 盗窃；盗窃物
[01:14.04]cripple [ˈkrɪpl]vt. 削弱；严重影响 例 Critics say that would cripple an already beleaguered economy.
[01:23.64]belated [bɪˈleɪtɪd]a. 延误的；延迟的 例 The French protest strikes led to a belated vote of the reform bill.
[01:33.72]honour [ˈɒnə(r)]vt. 信守，履行(承诺)；承兑远期票据 n. 信用；(用于客套语中)荣幸 搭 for the honour of 为了…的信誉 / give one's word of honour 用…的名誉担保 / on one's honour 以…的名誉担保
[01:48.12]efficiency [ɪˈfɪʃnsi]n. 效率；效能，功效 搭 efficiency apartment 〈美〉(有厨房和卫生设 备的)公寓小套间
[01:56.40]behalf [bɪˈhɑːf]n. 利益；方面；支持 例 On behalf of our staff, I express our sincere blessings to you. 搭 on behalf of 代表；为了
[02:07.68]antedate [ˌæntiˈdeɪt]vt. 早于，(在信、文件等上)写上比实 际日期早的日期；倒填日期；使提前发生 n. 比实 际日期早的日期 例 The invoice should be antedated to January 1st.
[02:20.76]discretion [dɪˈskreʃn]n. 判断力；谨慎，慎重 搭 at one's discretion 自行判断 / at the discretion of 任凭…处理
[02:30.00]preside [prɪˈzaɪd]vi. 担任会议主席；主持；主管，负责
[02:34.20]objective [əbˈdʒektɪv]n. 目标，目的 a. 客观(上存在)的 搭 objective reality 客观现实；客观存在
[02:41.88]mistime [ˌmɪsˈtaɪm]vt. 使不合时宜；在不当的时间做(或 说) 例 His behaviours at work mistimes him.
[02:50.28]rapacious [rəˈpeɪʃəs]a. 掠夺的；贪婪的
[02:53.76]dimension [daɪˈmenʃn]n. 方面；因素；[pl.] 长(或宽、高) 度；维度；规模，程度
[02:59.76]shortlist [ˈʃɔːtlɪst]n. 候选人名单 vt. 把…列入候选人名单 例 He was shortlisted as a candidate for sales manager. 搭 a shortlist for …的候选人名单
[03:12.36]whereby [weəˈbaɪ]ad. 靠，以…为手段 例 I have made a phone book whereby we can liaise with each other.
[03:21.72]attach [əˈtætʃ]vt. 扣押；系，连接；附加；贴上；委 例 Please attach these labels to your hand luggage.
[03:30.60]halve [hɑːv]vt. 把…分成两半；把…减半；对分，平摊 例 These impacts could halve the costs of dealing with climate change by the end of 2050.
[03:42.96]tortuous [ˈtɔːtʃuəs]a. 曲折的；拐弯抹角的；复杂的
[03:47.04]profitable [ˈprɒfɪtəbl]a. 有利可图的；能盈利的
[03:51.12]anticipate [ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt]v. 预期，期望；提前使用；提前偿 还；抢占…先机 例 Intervention itself is a sign of failure, a failure to anticipate the moment of crisis.
[04:05.52]alarming [əˈlɑːmɪŋ]a. 令人担忧的；使人惊恐的；惊人的 例 Internet addiction among the youngsters has increased to an alarming extent. 搭 at an alarming rate 达到惊人的速度
[04:20.64]asset [ˈæset]n. 资产；有用的东西；有利条件，优点 例 The higher inflation might drive more people to buy riskier assets.
[04:31.20]temptation [tempˈteɪʃn]n. 诱惑，引诱；诱惑物 搭 be surrounded by temptations 受到各种诱惑 / resist temptation 抵制诱惑
[04:41.52]benevolence [bɪˈnevələns]n. 捐款，捐助物；善意，善心 例 The government's policies of benevolence receive everyone's support.
[04:53.52]burden [ˈbɜːdn]n. 负担；责任，义务；重载 vt. 担负；使 负重 例 The adoption of this policy would relieve them of a tremendous burden.
[05:05.04]handle [ˈhændl]n. 柄状物；可抓握的东西 vt. 处理，办 理；管理，对待；经营，买卖 vi. 搬运；操纵 例 Unfortunately, nobody here knew how to handle a situation like this. 搭 fly off the handle 勃然大怒 / have a handle on 控制，掌握，驾驭
[05:23.64]motto [ˈmɒtəʊ]n. 箴言，格言；座右铭
[05:26.52]broker [ˈbrəʊkə(r)]n. 经纪人，代理人 例 You can sign up for automatic savings with your bank and broker online.
[05:36.96]avenue [ˈævənjuː]n. 途径，方法，渠道 例 The government instruction is the main avenue that modern economic regions form. 搭 avenue of infection 传染途径 / avenue to... …的途径
[05:53.04]trait [treɪt]n. 品质；特性；性格；少许，微量 例 China's huge market potential is undoubtedly the most attractive trait for many foreign firms. 搭 a trait of 少许
[06:07.56]integral [ˈɪntɪɡrəl]a. 构成整体所必需的；基本的；组成 的；完整的 例 Teams will start to approach customer interaction as an integral part of their development lifecycles. 搭 be integral to 对…来说是必需的
[06:25.68]challenge [ˈtʃælɪndʒ]n. 挑战；申请回避；艰巨的任务；怀 疑 vt. 向…挑战；对…质疑；对…表示异议 vi. 提 出挑战；反对，公然反抗 例 These costs can be justified only by the nature of the challenge.
[06:40.92]coefficient [ˌkəʊɪˈfɪʃnt]n. 协同因素；系数；折算率 例 The institutional change is the coefficient result of exogenous variables and endogenous variables.
[06:55.92]eliminate [ɪˈlɪmɪneɪt]vt. 排除；消除 搭 eliminate...from... 将…从…中消除
[07:02.64]overcapacity [ˌəʊvəkəˈpæsəti]n. 生产力过剩
[07:06.84]disparate [ˈdɪspərət]a. 毫不相干的；迥然不同的 例 The cultures of these two companies were so disparate that it is really hard for me to adapt to the new one.
[07:21.36]affirm [əˈfɜːm]v. 断言，肯定地说；确认；证实；批准 例 The applicant for the post affirms that all the information he provides is true and correct.
[07:34.56]spontaneous [spɒnˈteɪniəs]a. 自发的，自然产生的 例 We must be soberly aware that government reform is a passive adjustment rather than a spontaneous action.
[07:49.68]requisite [ˈrekwɪzɪt]a. 需要的；必要的 n. 必需品；必要条 件
[07:54.36]ergonomically [ˌɜːɡəˈnɒmɪkli]ad. 功效学地，人类工程学地 例 All of the office furniture in our company is ergonomically designed.
[08:06.60]ceiling [ˈsiːlɪŋ]n. 天花板；(价格、工资等)最高限额，上 限 例 Earlier this year, he led negotiations on raising the debt ceiling.
[08:18.00]roughshod [ˈrʌfʃɒd]a. 铁蹄上装有防滑钉的；残暴的 搭 ride roughshod over sb. 残暴地对待某人
[08:25.32]hospitality [ˌhɒspɪˈtæləti]n. 好客，殷勤；食宿招待 例 Their hospitality left a very good impression on the guests. 搭 hospitality room 迎宾室 / hospitality suite 会客室，接待处
[08:41.28]videoconference [ˈvɪdiəʊkɒnfərəns]n. 视频会议
[08:45.96]appoint [əˈpɔɪnt]vt. 任命，委任；指定(时间、地点)；指 定…为财产受益人 例 We will increase our turnover if you appoint us as your sole agent. 搭 appoint that sth. (shall) be done 命令完成某 事
[09:02.16]pander [ˈpændə(r)]vi. 迎合(他人的低级趣味或淫欲)；纵 容，迁就 例 The boss is good at pandering to the old staff without alienating the new ones. 搭 pander to 迎合；纵容
[09:16.56]ensure [ɪnˈʃʊə(r)]vt. 保证，担保；保护 例 We ensure that you will get the best quality with the lowest price. 搭 ensure sb. against/from loss 使某人不受损 失
[09:30.60]mechanism [ˈmekənɪzəm]n. 机械装置；机构；机制
[09:34.56]yearbook [ˈjɪəbʊk]n. 年鉴；年刊
[09:37.44]showpiece [ˈʃəʊpiːs]n. 展品；样品
[09:40.56]entrust [ɪnˈtrʌst]vt. 委托，托付；委托管理 例 He entrusted a big sum of money to our care. 搭 entrust sb. with sth. 委托某人某事
[09:51.48]expense [ɪkˈspens]n. 价钱；花费；[pl.] 开支，业务费 用；支付手段 例 The expense budget varies with the project. 搭 at sb.'s expense 由某人付费 / at the expense of 由…负担费用；以…为代价 / go to the expense of 为…目的而花钱，花钱于
[10:10.08]rebound [ˈriːbaʊnd]n. 反弹；回弹；重新振作 [rɪˈbaʊnd]vi. (使)弹回，(使)反弹 搭 on the rebound 在弹回之际
[10:18.72]gallery [ˈɡæləri]n. 长廊；楼座；画廊；展览馆；观众； 收集，聚集 例 The plan is to erect a seven-floor residential building that includes an art gallery. 搭 National Gallery 英国伦敦国家美术馆 / play to the gallery 迎合观众；哗众取宠 / press gallery 新闻记者席(指英国下议院)
[10:41.40]underperform [ˌʌndəpəˈfɔːm]vi. 表现不佳；工作不如预期(或同 行) 例 If you keep on pushing through the work, you'll eventually lose your focus, start to underperform, make mistakes and feel stressed out all the time.
[11:01.80]provision [prəˈvɪʒn]n. 供应；准备；条款，规定；[pl.] 供应 品；存粮 搭 with the provision that 以…为条件
[11:10.20]exemplify [ɪɡˈzemplɪfaɪ]vt. 举例证明，例示 例 Exemplifying is quite common to make an idea easily understood when explaining something at a meeting.
